==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Doge]]s spawn, delay 3.33~16.67 seconds<sup>100f~500f</sup>.
*1 [[Dark Emperor Nyandam]] spawns as the boss after 2 seconds<sup>60f</sup>.
*3 [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 2 seconds<sup>60f</sup>, delay 0.07~0.67 seconds<sup>2f~20f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 2 seconds<sup>60f</sup>, delay 13.33~20 seconds<sup>400f~600f</sup>.
*1 [[Ms. Sign]] spawns after 126.67 seconds<sup>3,800f</sup>.
*20 [[Assassin Bear]]s spawn after 133.33 seconds<sup>4,000f</sup>, delay 0.67~1.33 seconds<sup>20f~40f</sup>.

==Strategy==
The Assassin Bears are of a low enough magnification to be killed off by the [[Cat Cannon]], so 20 of them may not sound like a problem at first. However, the Cat Cannon won't catch all of them because they have a short spawn delay between each and the enemy limit in this stage is 10. Waiting for it to fire again is out of the question, so players are nearly '''required''' to beat the stage within a little more than two minutes.

While destroying the base is mostly trivial due to it having less than 100,000 health, the Dark Emperor Nyandam is no pushover, being buffed significantly in this stage with his health reaching nearly 3.8 million on 3-crown, and has more than enough damage to instantly kill whatever attackers in his range. Units who can force him to flinch (such Sniper, anything with the [[Knockback]] ability against Reds and the default Cat Cannon) can briefly disable his hitbox, so faster units can potentially move past him and destroy the base without having to eliminate him. [[Pirate Cat (Rare Cat)|Pirate Cat]] works best for this purpose while rushers like [[Crazed Cow Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Cow Cat]] and [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]] charge ahead.

Alternatively, if you do not want to [[cheese]] the stage, try to kill the group of Doge Darks as fast as possible with attackers like [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]], then spawn DPS units like [[Axe Cat (Normal Cat)|Dark Cat]], [[Crazed Axe Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Brave Cat]], [[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Island Cat]], [[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Whale Cat]] and other [[:Category:Anti-Red Cats|anti-Red]] cats with a similar [[Special Abilities|ability]], like [[Bath Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bath Cat]], to hopefully remove Nyandam with time to spare for the base. The aforementioned [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] can also speed things along.

